Title:
SquidC5 — Security-first AI-native C5 Teamserver (SquidSec)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- SquidC5 is an open-source red team/pentest teamserver (“C5”: Command, Control, Cognitive, Collaborative, Coordination) with an Ops web UI and operator CLI for managing sessions, listeners, payloads, and post-ex actions.  
- It focuses on “security-first” C2 operations: scoped API tokens, immutable audit hash chain with verification, engagement rules-of-engagement (ROE), and server-side human-in-the-loop (HITL) controls.  
- The project adds AI-assisted operations via INKO operator chat and an Admin AI, plus an optional restricted MCP (off by default) for external LLM clients with allow-listed tools and audited calls.  
- It includes a native Go implant (`sc5beacon`) supporting AEAD-protected communications, sleep/jitter/kill windows, file operations, and SOCKS reverse-dial pivoting, plus an “implant factory” build pipeline and malleable C2 profiles.  
- Useful primarily for authorized Red Teams and penetration testers who want a self-hosted, auditable C2 with collaboration features; also relevant to Blue Teams for understanding modern “AI-assisted” operator workflows and associated control points.  
- Interesting because it explicitly treats operator tooling/AI integration as a security boundary (capability gating, HITL, audit chain) rather than bolting AI onto a C2 without governance.

Technical Focus:
- Scoped bearer tokens, policy engine, and HITL enforcement
- Immutable audit hash chain and audit verification
- AI integration: INKO, Admin AI capability allow-lists, restricted MCP (JSON-RPC)
- Native Go beacon with AEAD, tasking, and operational controls (sleep/jitter/hours)
- SOCKS5 pivoting (reverse-dial duplex) and file operation APIs
- Malleable C2 profiles and transform pipelines (base64/xor/netbios/etc.)

Use Cases:
- Stand up a self-hosted teamserver (Docker or binary) for authorized red team engagements
- Generate/build implants and manage beacon sessions at scale via UI or CLI
- Enforce ROE (banned commands, end time) and require HITL approval for sensitive actions (e.g., file writes)
- Run SOCKS pivots through compromised hosts for internal network access
- Capture out-of-band interaction evidence via built-in OAST collaborator (DNS/HTTP/SMTP)
- Integrate controlled AI assistance for operator workflows while retaining auditability and tool gating

Keywords:
SquidC5, C2, teamserver, FastAPI, Ops UI, operator CLI, Go beacon, sc5beacon, AEAD, scoped tokens, audit hash chain, HITL, ROE, MCP, JSON-RPC, LLM integration, Ollama, SOCKS5 pivot, malleable C2 profiles, OAST collaborator